launch. That is unsupported. No evidence supports T1 being 'likely', and the dossier's Grenfell finding cuts against it. It recommends launching while the validating survey is still pending. The reversal condition is incoherent ('or if the difference is statistically significant'), and several fields are truncated."}}, "red_flags": [{"kind": "misleading_quote", "event_ids": ["A11"], "reason": "An exact quote of the Grenfell report finding that Kingspan created a false market for K15 is presented as supporting a fire-safety premium theory. This reverses its evident meaning, since it signals a reputational liability on fire safety."}, {"kind": "unsupported_inference", "event_ids": ["A11", "A12", "A14", "A17", "A18"], "reason": "Company financial and Grenfell reports are treated as support for homeowner purchase motives. T1 is rated 'likely' with no supporting evidence. The final recommendation asserts that 'safety-certified insulation provides compliance with fire codes' and a premium, stating hypotheses as fact."}, {"kind": "other", "event_ids": ["A15"], "reason": "A marketing claim ('a great DIY project') is counted as support for demand. It is also contradicted by kingspan-est-rafters ('This isn't a DIY job'), which was retrieved but never assessed."}, {"kind": "other", "event_ids": ["A4", "A13"], "reason": "Retrieved disconfirming evidence is ignored: 6.3% homeowner install intent, professional-only rafter installation, and an online-only third-party marketplace listing. Sources are also misclassified as independent_study (A11, A12, A14)."}, {"kind": "non_discriminating_test", "event_ids": ["A16"], "reason": "The measure scale is incoherent and the decision rule contradicts itself, mapping the same <5-point outcome to opposite actions. The results therefore cannot reliably separate the theories or drive the decision. The test also cannot detect absence of consumer demand."}], "suitable_for_training": false, "screen_reason": "The episode completed, but it fails screening on several critical errors. It misreads the Grenfell source to support a fire-safety premium (A11), makes unsupported inferences from company financial reporting (A12, A14), treats a marketing claim as evidence (A15), and ignores retrieved contradictory evidence (A13). Its test has an incoherent, self-contradictory decision rule (A16), and it ends in an unsupported launch recommendation (A18). Any single one of these would disqualify it."}
